{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-67571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/bb15327593f4452d177ac7d6fbd910c765c847874505b35a13bdd69b123242d0.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-67571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={45}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x+3}{2x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{x+3}{2x} \\\\ 2x & =x+3 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x+3=3+3=6, \\\\ AB & =2x=2(3)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-67571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "20bdeaa60bbfe022127ca37798860fd587ebb84017298d95e1b10b9c6b79478d"} {"question" "q-67571" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-67571" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "27"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-67571" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-244471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/6d32c4a97154570f8a66f89ba5fee46f11aa09d2cd152edb4aa05f2613d035f3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{3}{2},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-244471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & =\\frac{x+3}{3x-5} \\\\ 3(3x-5) & =2(x+3) \\\\ 9x-15 & =2x+6 \\\\ 7x & =21 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x-5=3(3)-5=4, \\\\ AC & =x+3=3+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-244471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "20bdeaa60bbfe022127ca37798860fd587ebb84017298d95e1b10b9c6b79478d"} {"question" "q-244471" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-244471" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/7e555f1574ba37c5b2ac8f4bca54f0d9e2b449e1351f792feba334ddbdc5b8df.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\sqrt{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\sqrt{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-4)}{8-x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(8-x) & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4) \\\\ 8-x & =x-4 \\\\ 2x & =12 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =8-x=8-6=2, \\\\ AC & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4)=\\sqrt{3}(6-4)=2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "20bdeaa60bbfe022127ca37798860fd587ebb84017298d95e1b10b9c6b79478d"} {"question" "q-251088" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251088" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/58af9726d81e1d926f814736fa92dc95c427d4346c40252470380f51a5fcf50a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ opposite to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{15}{BC} \\\\ BC & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\ BC & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =37.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "20bdeaa60bbfe022127ca37798860fd587ebb84017298d95e1b10b9c6b79478d"} {"question" "q-251125" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251125" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{75}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/assets/d792a93992bbd915063156e0c8fb4f65a71f1609cee5141609e4a5ca6ba6f405.png)\n\nThe **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠C={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠C,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠C) & =\\frac{AB}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(2x+1) & =3\\sqrt{3}(x-1) \\\\ 2x+1 & =3x-3 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{3}(x-1)=\\sqrt{3}(4-1)=3\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ BC & =2x+1=2(4)+1=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "20bdeaa60bbfe022127ca37798860fd587ebb84017298d95e1b10b9c6b79478d"} {"question" "q-251187" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"} {"question" "q-251187" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070169/state.json" "file_sha256" "e29cc82ac3302a2c5f47e27f4135fdb08e7558926061d0f6a049a03d6b41e122"}] "usage" {"q-244471" []} "basis" 2459 "retractions" [[17592186115483 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/q-244471.png)\n\nGiven that $\\tan (m∠B) = \\frac{3}{2}$, the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is {{field-1}} square units."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186232794] "immutable_fields" [[17592186112318 :answer-field/correct] [17592186112318 :answer-field/id] [17592186112318 :answer-field/key] 